<title>LITHUANIA: GOV'T TIGHTENS RULES FOR STATE-BACKED LOANS.</title>
<headline>GOV'T TIGHTENS RULES FOR STATE-BACKED LOANS.</headline>
<dateline>VILNIUS 1997-04-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Lithuanian government said on Thursday that it was tightening its supervision of companies that receive loans guaranteed by the state.</p>
<p>The government said in a statement that cabinet approval would be needed in cases where the state had to repay a company's debt from budgetary sources.</p>
<p>&quot;In every situation where a loan is not repaid, the case will be investigated, and an explanation will be provided by the ministry which suggested the loan,&quot; the statement said.</p>
<p>The statement added that for companies where private owners have a stake of at least 51 percent, a legal investigation will be carried out.</p>
<p>--Vilnius newsroom +370 2 22 35 17</p>
